From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OpenXR: keep the interaction profiles it creates, to free
 them

_load_action_map() meant to record each interaction profile it
creates so free_interaction_profiles() frees them later, but it checked
and appended to the action map's array instead of interaction_profiles,
and only when the profile was already there. None were recorded, so
none were freed, and every run that used OpenXR ended with "RID
allocations of type 'InteractionProfile' were leaked at exit".

Test: start OpenXR with the default action map and quit; no leaked
interaction profiles are reported.

Upstream: to propose (still in master).
---
diff --git a/godot/modules/openxr/openxr_interface.cpp b/godot/modules/openxr/openxr_interface.cpp
index 290257e..d8aa87a 100644
--- a/godot/modules/openxr/openxr_interface.cpp
+++ b/godot/modules/openxr/openxr_interface.cpp
@@ -386,8 +386,8 @@ void OpenXRInterface::_load_action_map() {
 				openxr_api->interaction_profile_suggest_bindings(ip);
 
 				// And record it in our array so we can clean it up later on
-				if (interaction_profile_array.has(ip)) {
-					interaction_profile_array.push_back(ip);
+				if (!interaction_profiles.has(ip)) {
+					interaction_profiles.push_back(ip);
 				}
 			}
 		}
